WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.102
So in many ways, you,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:02.869
at least for me,

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.471
you created

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.773
or defined American political satire.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.942
How has that changed?

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.543
It feels to me like the

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.012
the stuff you did,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:12.579
you know, the

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.747
the showing, the video

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.349
and then commenting, it's become it's

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.350
everybody does it.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.385
And it's not even

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:19.552
the it's not even comics.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.221
I mean, that's what Tucker Carlson does

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.422
when he wants to make his voice.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:22.822
Sure.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.224
He's his borrowing from your.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.092
Yes. Playbook. Yes.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:30.230
No, it's it's a real delight knowing oh,

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.500
it's always good to arm the most cynical

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.368
and worst people in media.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.403
But do you look at it and say,

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.103
now this whole thing

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.805
has commoditized you?

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.341
Well, it was listen, it was commoditized.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.477
You know, I wasn't doing it

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.012
out of gracious altruism.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.548
I mean, we were selling Budweiser.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.316
It's always been commoditized.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.852
It was I think it's

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.456
you know, there's a lot of talk of.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.224
So exposing absurdity

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.226
or exposing hypocrisy. What's the point?

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.196
The point is, is that

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.066
this is a relentless fight.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.700
They always talk about,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.635
you know, the

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.937
the arc of the moral universe is long,

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.572
but it bends towards justice,

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.074
but it doesn't bend towards justice

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.041
by gravity.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.509
Like, you have to bend it.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.544
And there's a bunch of people

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.045
trying to bend it back.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.082
And you use every tool in your arsenal,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.251
and none of them will be

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:25.819
you know,

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.088
the one thing there is no panacea.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.789
It takes, you know,

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.157
all those different things

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.258
doing in Washington over

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.326
these past few years

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.395
gave me a great understanding

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.198
of how things actually get done

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.899
incrementally and

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.935
and sometimes in one fell swoop.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.471
But our country is held together

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.973
by hundreds

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.542
of really talented legislative aides.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.412
Their bosses many times

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.816
are wind up dolls who really don't know.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.119
I mean, half of it, if you go down there,

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.587
especially the Senate,

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.522
is like an assisted living facility,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.457
like the intramural sports

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.060
at the Senate games.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.229
So, you know,

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.029
it's held together

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.030
by these legislative mates

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.800
that are relentlessly trying

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.934
to do the right thing

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.169
and by the thousands

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.670
of grassroots activists

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.906
that are trying to get access.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.908
And they're blocked by a mode

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.678
of lobby ists and moneyed interests

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.715
that prevent

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.050
the people in that building

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.720
from doing the work that best benefits

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:37.123
all the people outside of that building.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.526
And that's the process.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.194
So you have to use every tool.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:44.631
You have to permeate that force field.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.933
But presumably the people there

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.168
who are Republicans,

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.869
who are conservative Republicans,

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:50.436
those aides

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.871
think they're doing the right thing

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:52.605
and they're trying

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.307
to get across their there.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.141
But they're doing it.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.075
They're honest.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.177
Look, if you can find

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.311
honest brokers down there,

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.679
you can work with them.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.413
What I'm saying

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.981
is that forcefield around

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.151
it is made up of not honest brokers,

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:08.087
its moneyed interests, its lobbyists,

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.022
its people

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.823
who are weaponising misinformation

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.025
and disinformation

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.794
and all of those form this.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.996
It's the most cloistered.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.332
So you feel you found you could deal

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.434
with very conservative Republicans,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.936
force the book

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:23.903
because there was some way

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.471
to find common ground

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.973
people of good faith.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.675
Now, there were huge

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.343
disagreements about certain things.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:33.179
But when you found someone of good faith,

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.848
you could always get something done.

